// Pull request author: vl43den
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Self-Deletion Via Choice/Del Command Combination
// Sigma ID: 8b2a095d-5ce5-407a-b54c-7b299237a13a
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Vladan Sekulic
// Date: 2026-09-30 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070.004
// Description: Detects "cmd.exe" using "choice" with a timeout as a sleep, then "del"/"erase" to remove a file.
//   This is a common self-deletion one-liner used by .NET stealers and RATs, like SectopRAT, to
//   remove their own executable after exit.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate .NET Apps, uninstallers or updaters that self-delete using choice as a delay
// References:
//   - https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/uncovering-a-sectoprat-variant-embedded-in-legitimate-software
//   - https://tria.ge/221220-agsp7sbe5s/behavioral2
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/choice
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/67a926b7829419816f9c3096c30b1150d1e6deb5/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_choice_del_combined_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Cmd.Exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "choice " and ProcessCommandLine contains " /t ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "del " or ProcessCommandLine contains "erase ")
